# WN22-SO-000150: Windows Server 2022 Smart Card removal option must be configured to Force Logoff or Lock Workstation.
# Source: Windows Server 2022 STIG r8
# Severity: medium
# Generated from 01-extract/output/windows-server-2022-stig-r8-controls.json

META
    esp_id `win2022-wn22-so-000150-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `windows`
    criticality `high`

    title `Windows Server 2022 Smart Card removal option must be configured to Force Logoff or Lock Workstation.`
    description `Unattended systems are susceptible to unauthorized use and must be locked. Configuring a system to lock when a smart card is removed will ensure the system is inaccessible when unattended.`
    author `scanset-security`
    tags `windows,server-2022,stig,registry,reg-sz,medium,ksi-cmt-lmc,ksi-cmt-rmv,ksi-mla-evc,ksi-svc-acm`

    control_mapping `KSI:KSI-CMT-LMC,KSI:KSI-CMT-RMV,KSI:KSI-MLA-EVC,KSI:KSI-SVC-ACM,NIST-800-53:CM-6`
    control_objective `KSI-CMT-LMC,KSI-CMT-RMV,KSI-MLA-EVC,KSI-SVC-ACM`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `Windows:server-2022:endpoint`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `30`
    recommendation `Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration >> Windows Settings >> Security Settings >> Local Policies >> Security Options >> Interactive logon: Smart card removal behavior to "Lock Workstation" or "Force Logoff".`

    component_id `comp-windows-registry`

    impl_KSI_CMT_LMC `Windows Server implements KSI-CMT-LMC by setting registry value 'scremoveoption' (REG_SZ) under 'HKLM\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows NT\CurrentVersion\Winlogon' to the STIG-required value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match. Remediation sets the value via Group Policy or direct registry edit.`
    impl_KSI_CMT_RMV `Windows Server implements KSI-CMT-RMV by setting registry value 'scremoveoption' (REG_SZ) under 'HKLM\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows NT\CurrentVersion\Winlogon' to the STIG-required value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match. Remediation sets the value via Group Policy or direct registry edit.`
    impl_KSI_MLA_EVC `Windows Server implements KSI-MLA-EVC by setting registry value 'scremoveoption' (REG_SZ) under 'HKLM\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows NT\CurrentVersion\Winlogon' to the STIG-required value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match. Remediation sets the value via Group Policy or direct registry edit.`
    impl_KSI_SVC_ACM `Windows Server implements KSI-SVC-ACM by setting registry value 'scremoveoption' (REG_SZ) under 'HKLM\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows NT\CurrentVersion\Winlogon' to the STIG-required value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match. Remediation sets the value via Group Policy or direct registry edit.`
    impl_CM_6 `Windows Server implements CM-6 by setting registry value 'scremoveoption' (REG_SZ) under 'HKLM\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows NT\CurrentVersion\Winlogon' to the STIG-required value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match. Remediation sets the value via Group Policy or direct registry edit.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT target
        hive `HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE`
        key `SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows NT\CurrentVersion\Winlogon`
        name `scremoveoption`
        behavior executor powershell
    OBJECT_END

    STATE option_1
        exists boolean = true
        value string = `1`
    STATE_END

    STATE option_2
        exists boolean = true
        value string = `2`
    STATE_END

    CRI OR
        CTN registry
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF option_1
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
        CTN registry
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF option_2
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
